      <bpmn:task id="Bridge_2_1f6f" name="Here is the transition sentence connecting Process A and Process B:&#10;&#10;**Transition Sentence:**&#10;Once the IP approves the data request from the INQ, the Payment Office proceeds to execute the weekly vendor payment cycle. This triggers the subsequent generation of client invoices by the Accounts Receivable Department and the archiving of records by the Registry Office.&#10;&#10;***&#10;&#10;**Integrated Business Process Design**&#10;&#10;Based on your requirements, here is the **Vendor Payment and Client Invoicing Process** involving the specified roles and decision points. This process assumes the transition above has occurred (the payment is authorized/initiated).&#10;&#10;**Process Flow:**&#10;&#10;**1. Vendor Payment (Payment Office &amp; Vendor)**&#10;*   **Activity:** At the end of every week, the **Payment Office** generates a payment report and issues payment to the **Vendor**.&#10;*   **Output:** The Vendor receives payment and a payment notification.&#10;&#10;**2. Client Invoicing (Accounts Receivable Department &amp; Clients)**&#10;*   **Activity:** Upon confirmation of the vendor payment (or based on the weekly cycle), the **Accounts Receivable Department** generates monthly invoices for **Clients**.&#10;*   **Fee Application:** The department charges a service fee of **$35 per invoice**.&#10;*   **Notification:** The Client is notified of the invoice and the service fee.&#10;&#10;**3. Decision Point: Invoice Payment Status (Registry Office)**&#10;*   **Check:** The **Registry Office** monitors the status of the invoices sent to clients.&#10;*   **Decision:**&#10;    *   *Option A: Payment Pending.* The invoice remains open in the tracking system.&#10;    *   *Option B: Payment Received.* The invoice is marked as &quot;Paid.&quot;&#10;&#10;**4. Invoice Archiving (Registry Office)**&#10;*   **Condition:** This activity triggers only if the decision point results in **&quot;Payment Received.&quot;**&#10;*   **Activity:** The **Registry Office** selects the paid paper-based (or digital) invoices.&#10;*   **Action:** The invoices are archived systematically, first **per vendor** and then **per payment date**, and the payment tracking is finalized.&#10;&#10;***&#10;&#10;### Visual Summary of the Integrated Process&#10;&#10;1.  **[Decision/Trigger]**: Approval of Data Request (End of Process A)&#10;2.  **[Payment Office]**: Pay Vendor (Weekly)&#10;3.  **[Accounts Receivable Dept]**: Generate Client Invoice (+$35 Fee)&#10;4.  **[Registry Office]**: **CHECK** - Has the Client Paid the Invoice?&#10;    *   **NO** → Return to Tracking / Wait for Payment.&#10;    *   **YES** → **Archive Invoice** (Sorted by Vendor -&gt; Payment Date)." /><bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_P2B_2" sourceRef="atom_1_Task_3" targetRef="Bridge_2_1f6f" /><bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_B2C_2" sourceRef="Bridge_2_1f6f" targetRef="atom_2_sid-A5093785-9337-44F9-BA57-6837E2F0DA1B" /><bpmn:extensionElements />
